# Dishify — project TODO (through launch)

## Testing scripts (already in repo)

- [x] `backend/scripts/smoke_test_api.py` — health + POST /recommend
- [x] `backend/scripts/workflow_test.py` — register → login → prefs → recommend
- [x] `backend/scripts/index_recipes.py` — local Qdrant indexing (non-Docker)
- [ ] `backend/scripts/e2e_api_audit.py` — full endpoint + error-case audit (not yet written)
- [ ] Wire API tests into `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (CI only checks restriction_rules.json today)

Run:
```bash
python backend/scripts/smoke_test_api.py
python backend/scripts/workflow_test.py
```

---

## Phase 0 — Infra & data (mostly done)

- [x] Docker Compose: Postgres, Keycloak, Qdrant, microservices
- [x] Keycloak realm + clients (web, iOS, backend)
- [x] Qdrant indexing worker (`docker compose run --rm indexing-worker --recreate`)
- [x] 10k annotated dev dataset + restriction_rules.json
- [ ] Fix Qdrant Docker healthcheck (shows unhealthy but works)
- [ ] Document one-command bootstrap in README (`start.sh` + index + smoke test)

---

## Phase 1 — Backend MVP (mostly done)

- [x] Gateway: /health, /recommend, auth proxy, user proxy
- [x] Recommendation pipeline: retrieve → rank → explain
- [x] User service: register, login, /me, /me/preferences (Postgres)
- [x] Shared contracts (`dishify-contracts`) + ranking lib (`dishify-ranking`)
- [x] Hard-filter on exclusion_restrictions in Qdrant
- [x] Stored prefs applied on authenticated /recommend when body omits restrictions
- [ ] Remove or archive legacy monolith under `backend/app/` once fully migrated
- [ ] Gateway `/health` should reflect downstream dependency status (optional readiness probe)

---

## Phase 2 — Auth (backend wiring + production config)

- [ ] Set `DISABLE_AUTH=false` on gateway for staging/production
- [ ] Fix `GET /auth/config` public URLs (`KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL` → `localhost:9001` / prod domain, not `keycloak:9001`)
- [ ] Retest full flow with auth required on /recommend
- [ ] `POST /auth/refresh` — refresh-token exchange (post-MVP but needed before long sessions)
- [ ] `POST /auth/logout` — server-side or documented client-side Keycloak logout
- [ ] `POST /auth/forgot-password` — password reset flow
- [ ] Token expiry UX guidance for clients (access_token TTL = 300s)
- [ ] CORS: restrict origins in production (currently all origins in dev)
- [ ] Rate limiting on /auth/login and /recommend
- [ ] Secrets management (.env → prod vault / GitHub secrets)

---

## Phase 3 — Frontend (web)

- [ ] Scaffold / verify Vite + React app runs (`npm run dev`)
- [ ] API client: base URL, typed request/response (`docs/API.md`)
- [ ] Auth shell: login + register screens (`POST /auth/login`, `/auth/register`)
- [ ] Store JWT; attach `Authorization: Bearer` on all protected calls
- [ ] Protected routes (recommend, preferences require login)
- [ ] Preferences screen: GET/PUT `/me/preferences` (exclusion_restrictions picker from known tags)
- [ ] Recommend screen: query input, pantry/ingredient list, top_k
- [ ] Results UI: title, score, reasoning (+/−), directions, inventory matched/missing
- [ ] Loading / error states (401, 422, 503)
- [ ] Optional: PKCE via Keycloak (`dishify-web`) instead of password login
- [ ] `.env` for `VITE_API_URL`, Keycloak URLs
- [ ] Responsive layout + basic accessibility
- [ ] Connect to backend with `DISABLE_AUTH=false` before launch

